  "Question": "Betty used a calculator to find the product \\(0.075 \\times 2.56.\\) She forgot to enter the decimal points. The calculator showed \\(19200.\\) If Betty had entered the decimal points correctly, the answer would have been",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(0.0192\\)",
    "B": "\\(0.192\\)",
    "C": "\\(1.92\\)",
    "D": "\\(19.2\\)",
    "E": "\\(192\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "B",
  "Solution": "Omitting the decimal point changes \\(0.075\\) into \\(75\\), making it \\(1000\\) times as large. It changes \\(2.56\\) into \\(256\\), making it \\(100\\) times as large. Therefore the displayed product is \\(1000\\times100=100000\\) times the correct product.\n\nScale it back down:\n\\[\n19200\\div100000=0.19200=0.192.\n\\]\nThe answer is \\(\\boxed{\\text{B}}\\).",
